  m_Name: item_l39_occupancy_sensing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GlorifiedBody.Interaction.ItemDefinition
  itemId: l39_occupancy_sensing
  displayName: A FACILITIES NOTICE
  kind: 1
  drugType: 0
  colour: {r: 0.96, g: 0.95, b: 0.88, a: 1}
  description: a facilities notice.
  logText: "FACILITIES OFFICE \u2014 NOTICE TO SECURITY POSTS, FLOORS 1 AND 2\nRE:
    Occupancy sensing\n\nThe wireless access points in the ceilings now do two jobs.
    They carry the network, and they tell Azoth which rooms have people in them,
    so the lights, heat and air run only where someone is. This is where most of
    the energy saving comes from.\n\nIt works through walls and in the dark. It can
    tell a still person from an empty room, so the lights will no longer go out on
    you during a quiet shift.\n\nThis is not a camera. It records no picture. It
    is not a security system, and its data is not available at this post or for incident
    reports.\n\nBy hand: it also knows when you fall asleep at the desk. ask Dale"
  readFlag: 
  mapFloor: 
  audioClip: {fileID: 0}
  tapeLines: []
